# Line endings are not cosmetic in two places here, so they are pinned.
#
# SQLx checksums each migration file byte for byte. A migration applied from a
# CRLF checkout and then deployed from an LF one hashes differently, and the
# API refuses to start with "migration N was previously applied but has been
# modified". Nobody edited anything; git converted it.
*.sql text eol=lf

# A shell script with CRLF fails inside a Linux container with a message that
# names the wrong thing entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
